    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 11 with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands today\u2019s top efficiency score at 80.98. His favorable matchup against Irvin and the combination of an elite leadoff slot plus his high-upside speed profile makes him a core play as we aggressively hunt for steals in a tight league race. **Junior Caminero** (75.54) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.01) provide the elite power floor, with **Junior Caminero** benefiting significantly from an assumed #3 order spot and park factors, while **Yordan Alvarez** overcomes a neutral L/L platoon to remain a must-start due to his elite xwOBA and favorable wind conditions out of the park. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (69.06) as he exploits a favorable matchup against Buehler, rounding out a top-heavy offensive core.\n\nThe primary bench decision for this slate involved **Carson Benge** (52.26), who fell just shy of the active roster threshold. While his SP skill bonus against P\u00e9rez was noteworthy, the high scoring density of our outfield and utility spots\u2014specifically the platoon-heavy advantages for **Nelson Velazquez** and **Lars Nootbaar**\u2014pushed **Carson Benge** to the pine. We are monitoring the status of **Caleb Durbin**, whose score of 43.26 is depressed by a difficult matchup against Cease; while he is currently active, his status as a \"Lineup Pending\" player is a risk, and we remain ready to pivot if his order position slips further down the card. With **Casey Schmitt** confirmed on the IL and **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Gary Sanchez** unavailable, our focus remains on maximizing the efficiency of our active starters to protect our game caps while securing the necessary counting stats.",
